From 36096ace87fea3c206d8323431f433ae9245cc41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:24:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: the stand-in's Dock makes room for a window that goes
 into it, as hosted Macs were recorded
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On a Mac a Dock that is full gets smaller when a window goes into it and larger when one leaves, and the visible frame changes with it. The
stand-in's minimize said nothing of the displays. From 826 recordings, 164 minimizes and restores that stand alone:

- A Dock lower than 78 points changed its size at every one that could be seen: 100 of 100 on 1024×768, 4 of 4 on 1600×900. One of 78, its
  full size, at 8 of 56.
- By 2 points at the bottom, by 1 at a side; in one step, with one word of macOS's about its screens, at which its list is new. The restore
  undid it to the point, 50 of 50.
- A window that goes in mostly speaks while macOS still has the old list (36 of 54), one that comes out under the new (50 of 58). The other
  order can be asked for: both were recorded within one script.
- Arbor is told as the Accessibility layer tells it, 0.35 s after the word in the middle. No time passes at the act: the news comes later, on
  the harness's clock, and the wait is let go at every further word, as the real one is.

It is played where the main display has a Dock lower than 78, which the stand-in's own display has not. That such a Dock is full is a guess
where a person has made it small. It is switched off in the chaos lab, where no old seed is to walk another way, in the fake Mac of
the rehearsals, whose display is a constant so far, and in the replay of a trace, which has what the Dock did. So for now it plays
in its own tests and for whoever gives a harness such a display.

`changeDisplaysAsAMacDoes`, `setDisplays` and `stop` let go of news that is on its way.

What Arbor makes of it is pinned as it is: the docked neighbour of a window that goes into the Dock takes the room at once, by the visible frame
macOS still had, and gets 2 points more when Arbor hears of the Dock: 23 of the 42 recorded minimizes at which a neighbour moved. By
the project's measures 2 points are no move. Decided: known, and left (board 1.61).
